questions.explanation:
**Given:**

In quadrilateral PQRS, &ang;Q + &ang;S = 150&ordm;

Measures of &ang;P and &ang;R are in the ratio 4:3

**Formula Used:**

Sum of interior angles of a quadrilateral = 360&ordm;

**Calculation:**

Let &ang;P = 4x and &ang;R = 3x

&ang;P + &ang;Q + &ang;R + &ang;S = 360&ordm;

4x + 3x + 150&ordm; = 360&ordm;

7x + 150&ordm; = 360&ordm;

&rArr; 7x = 360&ordm; - 150&ordm;

&rArr; 7x = 210&ordm;

&rArr; x = 30&ordm;

&ang;R = 3x = 3 × 30&ordm; = 90&ordm;

**The measure of &ang;R is 90&ordm;.**

